/-! # Vanishing of cohomology for nontrivial algebraically trivial line modules

Source: Mumford, Abelian Varieties, II §8, property (vii), pp.76–77; properties
(i) and (vi), pp.75–76, relate the Picard-zero condition to algebraic equivalence.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-abelian-picard-zero-cohomology)

Cohomology means the right derived functors of global sections in modules on the
Zariski ringed space. The statement includes degree zero and every characteristic.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits MonoidalCategory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A nontrivial algebraically trivial invertible module on an abelian variety over an
algebraically closed field has vanishing coherent Zariski cohomology in every degree.
Algebraic equivalence is the equivalence relation generated by invertible-module families
over connected smooth parameter varieties, as in polarization calculus.

Source: Mumford, Abelian Varieties, II §8 (i), (vi), (vii), pp.75–77.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-abelian-picard-zero-cohomology)

Proof:
1. By lem-sc-abelian-variety-characterization, lem-sc-av-commutative and the proper and
smooth hypotheses, A is geometrically integral and commutative. Apply
lem-sfb-abelian-space-poincare-calculus over Spec k. Its hypotheses hold: the base is
locally Noetherian, A is proper and smooth, and smoothness and quasi-compactness give
finite presentation. Algebraic triviality holds after every algebraically closed field
extension: base-change every link of the defining equivalence chain. The parameter
varieties stay smooth by lem-sbc-smooth-relative-dimension-permanence and connected by
lem-weil-separably-closed-geometrically-connected (k is separably closed by
 def-pc-separably-closed). Choose a basis of L at the identity to rigidify it. The
representing property gives a point b of the dual with L isomorphic to the Poincare
fibre at b. Its first biadditivity identity, restricted to b, gives
m*L isomorphic to p1*L tensor p2*L on the ordinary Zariski product A times A.
2. Pull this identity back along x ↦ (x,-x). Pullback composition
(lem-pc-module-pullback-identity-composition) and tensor compatibility
(lem-weil-pbc-module-pullback-tensor) give L tensor [-1]*L isomorphic to O_A,
using the chosen basis of L at zero to identify its constant zero pullback.
3. A nonzero global section s of L is nonzero generically since A is integral and L
is locally free of rank one. The section s tensor [-1]*s is thus a nonzero global
function under step 2. By lem-pc-h0-proper-variety(2), that function is a nonzero
scalar. In each local frame the two coefficients have unit product, so each is a
unit. Hence s trivializes L, contradicting nontriviality. Thus H^0(A,L) vanishes.
4. Induct strongly on n. For n > 0, lem-sc-picard-kunneth-qcoh identifies degree-n
cohomology of p1*L tensor p2*L with the sum over p+q=n of H^p(A,L) tensor H^q(A,L).
The hypotheses hold: L is quasi-coherent, A is quasi-compact and separated by
properness, and its closed diagonal is affine by
lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-integral-separated-uc(b). Each summand vanishes since
p<n or q<n. By step 1, H^n(A times A,m*L) therefore vanishes.
5. The section j(x)=(x,0) of m satisfies m composed with j equal to the identity.
The canonical pullback comparisons and lem-weil-pbc-module-cohomology-fmap-functorial
make pullback along m followed by pullback along j the identity on H^n(A,L).
It factors through the zero module from step 4, so that identity is zero. Thus
H^n(A,L) vanishes, completing the induction. No characteristic or dimension
restriction is used; in dimension zero the nontriviality hypothesis has no instance. -/
theorem IsAbelianVariety.isZero_moduleCohomology_of_algebraicallyTrivial_nontrivial
    {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    (A : Over (Spec (.of k))) [GrpObj A] [IsAbelianVariety A]
    (L : A.left.Modules) [L.IsInvertible]
    (algebraicallyTrivial : Scheme.Modules.AreAlgebraicallyEquivalent A L (𝟙_ A.left.Modules))
    (nontrivial : ¬ Nonempty (L ≅ 𝟙_ A.left.Modules))
    (i : ℕ) : IsZero ((RingedSpace.moduleCohomology A.left.toRingedSpace i).obj L) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
